      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "54f2ba0bdfc9ed4495c644020620a3c6d8a5705e6e2374b65d1fa934564f046b"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "In effect, $ \\mathbf{V}^{1/2} $ is the square root of a matrix, in that, when squared, we recover $ \\mathbf{V} $. Denoting the inverse of $ \\mathbf{V}^{1/2} $ as $ \\mathbf{V}^{-1/2} $, we have the following properties",
      "source_page": 853,
      "printed_page": 833,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_appendix1:p035:b8"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        54.0,
        656.0,
        1010.0,
        729.0
      ],
      "source_pages": [
        853
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          54.0,
          656.0,
          1010.0,
          729.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "f4aed106c5581b15c875a894a03c01e5ddb70fa0e8d863912f2bd36a9c44d490"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "[[FORMULA:Genetics_appendix1_formula131]]",
      "source_page": 853,
      "printed_page": 833,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_appendix1:p035:b10",
        "Genetics_appendix1:p035:b9"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        107.0,
        743.0,
        871.0,
        784.0
      ],
      "source_pages": [
        853
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          917.0,
