        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "f589813ae5fa602d40a8871589a3d4133ddedb88880fa58c221733cb79c3a20a"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "[[FORMULA:Genetics_appendix1_formula132]]",
      "source_page": 853,
      "printed_page": 833,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_appendix1:p035:b13",
        "Genetics_appendix1:p035:b14"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        232.0,
        935.0,
        840.0,
        972.0
      ],
      "source_pages": [
        853
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          232.0,
          935.0,
          840.0,
          972.0
        ],
        [
          932.0,
          942.0,
          1007.0,
          973.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "77d62a0eec272acbc87d34cc7b26e4a1ec077aeca9b4e058648bc47068d934b2"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "Thus, the transformed variables have unit variance and are uncorrelated. Suppose y is an $ n \\times 1 $ column vector with $ y \\sim \\text{MVN}(\\mu, \\mathbf{V}) $. It follows that",
      "source_page": 853,
      "printed_page": 833,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_appendix1:p035:b15"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        53.0,
        985.0,
        1011.0,
        1051.0
      ],
      "source_pages": [
        853
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          53.0,
          985.0,
          1011.0,
          1051.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "5164bf6700b639ffde9bca8a8f8423608bad005625a84d783d44df5beea86cff"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "[[FORMULA:Genetics_appendix1_formula133]]",
      "source_page": 853,
      "printed_page": 833,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_appendix1:p035:b13",
        "Genetics_appendix1:p035:b14",
        "Genetics_appendix1:p035:b16"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        338.0,
        1070.0,
        724.0,
        1108.0
      ],
      "source_pages": [
        853
      ],
      "source_bboxes": [
        [
          232.0,
          935.0,
          840.0,
          972.0
        ],
        [
          932.0,
          942.0,
          1007.0,
          973.0
        ],
        [
          338.0,
          1070.0,
          724.0,
          1108.0
        ]
      ],
      "provenance_score": 1.0,
      "content_sha256": "fb691bb27c2571c8bd59244cfa8572dc3121c4cdb6c61fc00fcb392b68643e3f"
    },
    {
      "type": "discussion",
      "content": "so that $ z_{i} \\sim \\mathrm{N}(0,1) $, and hence the transformed variables are independent unit normals. Thus,",
      "source_page": 853,
      "printed_page": 833,
      "source_block_ids": [
        "Genetics_appendix1:p035:b17"
      ],
      "bbox": [
        50.0,
